.TH AROPAPER 1 2026-09-27 "aro 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aropaper \- draw a wallpaper on every screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aropaper
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aropaper
draws
.I file
as the wallpaper on every screen, at each screen's exact resolution,
covering it and cropping what does not fit.
It reads anything gdk-pixbuf can: PNG, JPEG, WebP, and SVG when librsvg is
installed.
With no
.IR file ,
it draws aro's own wallpaper: the SVG when an SVG loader is available,
otherwise the bundled 4K PNG.
.PP
.BR aro (1)
runs it by itself, following the
.B wallpaper
setting in
.BR aro (5),
so there is rarely a reason to start it by hand there.
Started by hand under aro anyway, it hands the file to aro, as
.B aroctl wallpaper
would, and exits: aro's own aropaper switches to it, and no second one runs.
It is an ordinary layer-shell client, so it also works on other compositors
with wlr-layer-shell, such as sway, Hyprland, niri and river.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-thumbnails
For aro's wallpaper picker: read lines of
.IR source ,
a tab and
.I thumb
on standard input, write a small PNG of each
.I source
to
.IR thumb ,
covering 960x540 like the wallpaper covers a screen, and print each
.I thumb
once it is written, with a
.B !
before it when
.I source
could not be read.
aro runs it; there is no need to by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/backgrounds/aro/
aro's wallpapers:
.BR aro-wallpaper ,
.BR aro-wallpaper-dwindle ,
.B aro-wallpaper-rim
and
.BR aro-wallpaper-lenses ,
each as an SVG and as PNGs at 1920x1080, 2560x1440 and 3840x2160.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when it was stopped normally, 1 when the file is missing or unreadable,
or no compositor could be reached.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aro (1),
.BR aro (5)
